.TH DQL-TOOLS 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-tools \- ad-hoc data munging: query JSON, CSV, and files with DelightQL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql tools jstruct
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I QUERY
.br
.B dql tools csvstruct
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I QUERY
.br
.B dql tools filemunge
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.BI \-\-table " SPEC PATH"
\&...
.I QUERY
.PP
Aliases:
.BR "dql t j" ", " "dql t c" ", " "dql t m" .
.SH DESCRIPTION
Three entry points that load external data into an ephemeral database
and run one DelightQL query against it, in the spirit of
.BR jq (1)
and
.BR awk (1).
.SS jstruct
Reads JSON from stdin and exposes it as the single-column relation
.BR j(j\ TEXT) ;
the query addresses the JSON through DelightQL's path and destructure
operators.
.SS csvstruct
Reads CSV from stdin and exposes it as the relation
.BR c(...) .
Without
.B \-\-has\-headers
the columns are named
.BR c1 ", " c2 ", ..."
.PP
CSV carries no types; each field acquires its value when it is staged.
Every column is declared with SQLite's NUMERIC affinity: a field that is a
well-formed integer or real literal is stored as that number and any other
field as text, so
.B "age > 26"
compares the values and a text literal compared with such a column is
converted the same way
.RB ( "age = \(dq30\(dq"
matches the number 30). An empty field is an absent value and is stored
as NULL; it qualifies for no comparison. A blank line in a one\-column
input is one empty field and therefore one NULL record; in a wider input a
blank line is not a record and is skipped. The affinity is the engine's
reading: it also converts
.BR 007 ", " "\(dq 30 \(dq"
and
.B 1e3
to numbers, and a column mixing numeric and non-numeric spellings compares
each cell by its own storage class.
.SS filemunge
Loads one relation per
.B \-\-table
spec from files, then runs the query against them. CSV and TSV tables are
staged under the same value law as
.BR csvstruct ;
a json\-singleton table is
.BR name(j\ TEXT) .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-table " SPEC PATH"
(filemunge) Table spec of the form
.IR name : format [: noheader ]
followed by the file path. Formats:
.BR csv ,
.BR tsv ,
.BR json\-singleton .
csv/tsv default to a header row; add
.B :noheader
to override. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-has\-headers
(csvstruct) Treat the first row as column headers.
.TP
.BI \-\-delimiter " CHAR"
(csvstruct) Field delimiter; default comma.
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-format " FORMAT"
Output format. Unlike
.BR dql-query (1),
the default here is
.BR table .
.TP
.BI \-\-to " STAGE"
Inspect instead of executing; same values and the same law as
.BR dql-query (1):
a compile stage renders, a digest stage runs only an effect-free query,
and
.B results
(the default) executes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ echo '[{"name":"Alice","age":30}]' | dql tools jstruct 'j(j)'
$ cat people.csv | dql tools csvstruct --has-headers 'c(*), age > 26'
$ printf 'Alice,30\en' | dql tools c 'c(*) |> (c1)'
$ dql tools filemunge --table people:csv people.csv \e
      --table orders:csv orders.csv \e
      'people(*), orders(*.(id))'
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-query (1)
